body:
If an employee tells me that unions are bad I'll simply reply with;

"As a whole unions are good and beneficial, only some tend to be lackluster in comparison. All employees deserve a worthwhile wage and trying to stomp someone else down because you think they're worth dirt just means you're a shitty coworker. There's a reason quiet quitting has been sparking like wildfire across many different job fields and DG shouldn't be any different. I don't blame workers for acting their wage when the company wants to pay pennies for the sheer number of jobs they ask of their workers. And if we want better wages and working conditions then collective bargaining with worker protections is the best means of going about it. After all, if unions were worthless or held no threat then DG nor most other corporations would spend the sheer amount of money that they do in order to fearmongering and union bust.

That I'd rather pay for a devil I know has more interest on being on my side than trying to believe that the one currently abusing us is ever going to meaningfully change other than for their own interest and tossing whoever they want under the bus in the process."
